          <section>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 mt-12">Plan for December, Not July</h2>

            <p>
              A solar camera that runs fine in August tells you very little about December 21, when Seattle gets eight and a half hours of daylight, the sun peaks at 19 degrees, and rain falls on most days of the month. Ask what the setup does on the fifth gray day, where the backup charging comes from and who is watching the battery. Park it in the open with a clear view of the southern sky. Then give the rest of the site the same attention: gates, lights on photocells, materials put away, and a call list that covers the holidays.
            </p>
            <br>

